+// With byte paint alpha on, the opacity a group hands on and this node's own
+// are folded into one paint's alpha wherever they affect one atomic draw: a
+// shape with a fill or a stroke but not both, and no filter, as
+// `applyOpacity` folds a leaf's, and a group whose one child is such a shape,
+// or another such group (`kMeoFoldsIntoChild`). A browser folds a group over
+// one draw so, and rounds the product once; rounding the group's layer and
+// the paint apart rounds twice. Anything else takes the product as a layer.
+void SkSVGRenderContext::meoApplyOpacity(SkScalar opacity, uint32_t flags, bool hasFilter) {
+    const float total = fDeferredPaintOpacity * SkTPin(opacity, 0.0f, 1.0f);
+    fDeferredPaintOpacity = 1;
+    if (total >= 1) {
+        return;
+    }
+
